[[ ## reasoning ## ]]
To identify adjectives, I will utilize the Natural Language Toolkit (nltk) library. I will tokenize each string, tag parts of speech, and filter for those labeled as adjectives (JJ). A Counter object will track occurrences.

[[ ## response ## ]]
import nltk
from collections import Counter

def get_adjectives(texts):
    adj_count = Counter()
    for text in texts:
        words = text.split()
        tags = nltk.pos_tag(words)
        for word, tag in tags:
            if tag == 'JJ':
                adj_count[word.lower()] += 1
    return dict(adj_count)

